<blockquote>
  <p><strong>Senior Engineer Takeaway:</strong> A beautiful design that takes 4 seconds to load on mobile loses 50% of its visitors before the first headline renders. True luxury web engineering blends striking kinetic aesthetics with sub-second performance.</p>
</blockquote>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
<h3>Can I migrate from an AI builder to custom code later?</h3>
<blockquote>
  <p>Most AI builders do not allow clean source code export; they either output minified, unmaintainable spaghetti code or lock your assets within their proprietary CMS. Migrating later almost always requires a complete ground-up rebuild.</p>
</blockquote>

<h3>Is custom web development significantly more expensive than AI builders?</h3>
<blockquote>
  <p>Initially, an AI builder subscription seems cheaper. However, when factoring in lost conversions from slow loading times, poor SEO rankings, third-party plugin subscription costs, and eventual rebuild expenses, custom engineering yields a vastly higher return on investment over a 12-month period.</p>
</blockquote>

<h3>How do you achieve 100/100 Lighthouse scores with heavy animations?</h3>
<blockquote>
  <p>By using GPU-accelerated composited transforms (<code>transform: translate3d</code>), strict layout dimensions on all media assets, responsive WebP/SVG vector assets, and decoupling kinetic animations from the main UI thread via GSAP and Lenis virtual scrolling.</p>
</blockquote>
